(908276, 104842, 6999, '<td valign="top">I can see the hard lines of your selection around the smoke, adn that foils the effect. Use of levels, or curves would make the desired effect easier i think, and from the look of this you also need a deeper depth of field - very little is in focus - or you need a faster shutter speed - if it''s motion blur. I know from my own experience that it''s very tricky with smoke ... but my sympathy for your attempt grants you a few points.</td>', 'I can see the hard lines of your selection around the smoke, adn that foils the effect. Use of levels, or curves would make the desired effect easier i think, and from the look of this you also need a deeper depth of field - very little is in focus - or you need a faster shutter speed - if it''s motion blur. I know from my own experience that it''s very tricky with smoke ... but my sympathy for your attempt grants you a few points.', '2004-09-13 19:47:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(908281, 104871, 6999, '<td valign="top">I like this, though I wish you hadn''t proveided such a mundane title for it. It has a feeling of landscape about it - which, in my opinion, is the secret of all near-figrative photography that isn''t people-based. It reminds me of aurora shots, and in it''s forms recalls the trumpets of Michelangelo''s heralds. The composition is startlingly effective too. 9</td>', 'I like this, though I wish you hadn''t proveided such a mundane title for it. It has a feeling of landscape about it - which, in my opinion, is the secret of all near-figrative photography that isn''t people-based. It reminds me of aurora shots, and in it''s forms recalls the trumpets of Michelangelo''s heralds. The composition is startlingly effective too. 9', '2004-09-13 19:51:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(908291, 104490, 18080, '<td valign="top">Really nice shot.<br/>B&amp;W works.<br/>Now is it Steve or Gordon.<br/>Or maybe i''m way off.<br/>High score anyway.<br/>The fence in the foreground really leads you through the image.<br/>Good luck</td>', 'Really nice shot.B&W works.Now is it Steve or Gordon.Or maybe i''m way off.High score anyway.The fence in the foreground really leads you through the image.Good luck', '2004-09-13 20:04:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(908296, 104016, 6999, '<td valign="top">Two Towers, huh? Simple, elegant, and ... well, just a touch bland for me. A bit obvious, you know? I''m sure it was difficult to shoot and all that, but that should never be a consideration in my book. A heap better than most others however. 8</td>', 'Two Towers, huh? Simple, elegant, and ... well, just a touch bland for me. A bit obvious, you know? I''m sure it was difficult to shoot and all that, but that should never be a consideration in my book. A heap better than most others however. 8', '2004-09-13 20:10:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(908300, 104914, 6999, '<td valign="top">Some enormously serious sharpening gone on here, huh? was that to get the smoke trails some definition? If so, selecting their area and then sharpening that would have prevented those very strong jaggies on the sticks themselves. It''s unfortunate, and ruins a fine effort.</td>', 'Some enormously serious sharpening gone on here, huh? was that to get the smoke trails some definition? If so, selecting their area and then sharpening that would have prevented those very strong jaggies on the sticks themselves. It''s unfortunate, and ruins a fine effort.', '2004-09-13 20:12:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(908305, 104776, 6999, '<td valign="top">excellent definition, even if your exposure/brightening has gone a touch too far in places IMO. Including the source might have given the image some sense of contet, instead of being simply a pretty pattern.</td>', 'excellent definition, even if your exposure/brightening has gone a touch too far in places IMO. Including the source might have given the image some sense of contet, instead of being simply a pretty pattern.', '2004-09-13 20:13:55.000000', NULL, 1),
