(910321, 103930, 3102, '<td valign="top">Great journalistic image, although I might have liked to have seen more of the burning object (despite the fact that "smoke" is the challenge). - 7</td>', 'Great journalistic image, although I might have liked to have seen more of the burning object (despite the fact that "smoke" is the challenge). - 7', '2004-09-15 01:00:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(910739, 104503, 6388, '<td valign="top">not sure why you shot the bottle with the label on the side like that...seems odd for a perfectly centred subject.  uber cool smoke effect - the long exposure worked very well 8</td>', 'not sure why you shot the bottle with the label on the side like that...seems odd for a perfectly centred subject.  uber cool smoke effect - the long exposure worked very well 8', '2004-09-15 04:27:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(910747, 104799, 6388, '<td valign="top">the toast is a welcome addition to the challenge...a lot of entries are just smoke...not too interesting.  this is nice...lighting could use some work; maybe a little directional light from behind the camera (like a spotlight or a halogen) to catch some highlights in the smoke. very nice shot.</td>', 'the toast is a welcome addition to the challenge...a lot of entries are just smoke...not too interesting.  this is nice...lighting could use some work; maybe a little directional light from behind the camera (like a spotlight or a halogen) to catch some highlights in the smoke. very nice shot.', '2004-09-15 04:31:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(910753, 103484, 6388, '<td valign="top">man I love doing that :) Well timed pic...I wonder if you used a wide angle and cropped, or did a burst of shots, or just got lucky? :)  very nice effect...P likes it :) 8</td>', 'man I love doing that :) Well timed pic...I wonder if you used a wide angle and cropped, or did a burst of shots, or just got lucky? :)  very nice effect...P likes it :) 8', '2004-09-15 04:32:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(910761, 104853, 6388, '<td valign="top">I''d have set this back from the background a bit, and then backlit the candle itself, rather than the wall - 2 reasons: 1) then the smoke would be going into darkness which would make for some really cool contrast and make you smoke stnd out more, and b) then you''d eliminate the shadow cast by the candle and holder.  solid effort.</td>', 'I''d have set this back from the background a bit, and then backlit the candle itself, rather than the wall - 2 reasons: 1) then the smoke would be going into darkness which would make for some really cool contrast and make you smoke stnd out more, and b) then you''d eliminate the shadow cast by the candle and holder.  solid effort.', '2004-09-15 04:40:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(910765, 103661, 6388, '<td valign="top">i bet that sweater smells awesome :S  little harsh lighting onthe hands...you''re getting a few blown highlights.  nice lighting on the face, and interesting concept.  Using multi-directional lighting (3 sources or more) would soften some of the shadows and bring back some of the models features.</td>', 'i bet that sweater smells awesome :S  little harsh lighting onthe hands...you''re getting a few blown highlights.  nice lighting on the face, and interesting concept.  Using multi-directional lighting (3 sources or more) would soften some of the shadows and bring back some of the models features.', '2004-09-15 04:42:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(910767, 105004, 6388, '<td valign="top">including the hand and face is a great idea.  lots of matches out there...but this is unique.  nice job.</td>', 'including the hand and face is a great idea.  lots of matches out there...but this is unique.  nice job.', '2004-09-15 04:43:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(910772, 105148, 6388, '<td valign="top">you''re taking a chance with the title given the site''s TOS, but it''s a) cool, b) Canadian, and c) only suggestive, not literal, so maybe you''ll get away with it.  good concept, a little weak in the llighting department.  Perhaps a darker background would have allowed you to cast more light directly at the bottle.  it''s hard to get rid of highlights and reflections and still give adequate light.  good effort.</td>', 'you''re taking a chance with the title given the site''s TOS, but it''s a) cool, b) Canadian, and c) only suggestive, not literal, so maybe you''ll get away with it.  good concept, a little weak in the llighting department.  Perhaps a darker background would have allowed you to cast more light directly at the bottle.  it''s hard to get rid of highlights and reflections and still give adequate light.  good effort.', '2004-09-15 04:46:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(910777, 104803, 6388, '<td valign="top">nice job keeping the hands steady in the long exposure.  well executed, and decent composition.  love the concept.</td>', 'nice job keeping the hands steady in the long exposure.  well executed, and decent composition.  love the concept.', '2004-09-15 04:48:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(910964, 105072, 15497, '<td valign="top">EddyG for sure. If this doesn''t take the blue ribbon, I don''t know who will :-) Good Luck EddyG!</td>', 'EddyG for sure. If this doesn''t take the blue ribbon, I don''t know who will :-) Good Luck EddyG!', '2004-09-15 07:32:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(911000, 105072, 10858, '<td valign="top">Wow! :-) Creative idea, amazing implemetation! I am very curious about the description of this photo! The smoke is wonderful clear, composition with the increasing matches is great. But my favourite thing here is the shades of RGB colours! 10! 10! 10!</td>', 'Wow! :-) Creative idea, amazing implemetation! I am very curious about the description of this photo! The smoke is wonderful clear, composition with the increasing matches is great. But my favourite thing here is the shades of RGB colours! 10! 10! 10!', '2004-09-15 07:51:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(911016, 104430, 10858, '<td valign="top">Wonderful sharp photo, I also love the colours. :-) I think though, the browns on the bottom are too much, I would crop about 28-30% of the photo, and keep 1/2 - 1 cm of the smoke-stick holder. (8)</td>', 'Wonderful sharp photo, I also love the colours. :-) I think though, the browns on the bottom are too much, I would crop about 28-30% of the photo, and keep 1/2 - 1 cm of the smoke-stick holder. (8)', '2004-09-15 07:55:26.000000', NULL, 1),
